cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation data, please cite it as below."
title: "kotlin-mcp: Structural Code Summaries for LLM Context, with Evaluation Data"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Muchamad
    family-names: Mafmudin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7133-860X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fordewe/fojako"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  kotlin-mcp is an MCP server that parses Kotlin and Java with tree-sitter and
  reduces each file to its declarations: package and imports, type
  declarations, method signatures with annotations and visibility, and
  properties. It discards method bodies, comments, formatting, and generated
  sources. The repository also holds the tasks, model responses, judge and
  human scores, and analysis scripts behind the paper "Structural Code
  Summarization as a Context Strategy for LLM-Assisted Development: A
  Task-Based Evaluation under a Token Budget". The code is under the MIT
  License; the evaluation data is under ODC-By 1.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
keywords:
  - Android
  - Kotlin
  - code summarization
  - LLM
  - token optimization
  - tree-sitter
  - MCP
  - LLM-as-a-judge
